      "message": "In the very least we need some other tests, like:\n\n* Use \"i2cset -f -y 0 0x1b 0x21 0x0f\"\n* Power up system: it should power back up\n* Use \"i2cset -f -y 0 0x1b 0x21 0x0f\"\n* Press refresh-power: system should reboot\n* Use \"i2cset -f -y 0 0x1b 0x2a 0x00\"\n* Shut down and power back up.\n* Use \"i2cget -f -y 0 0x1b 0x2a\".  Confirm back to 0xff.\n* Use \"i2cset -f -y 0 0x1b 0x2a 0x00\"\n* Press refresh-power: system should reboot\n* Use \"i2cget -f -y 0 0x1b 0x2a\".  Confirm back to 0xff.\n\nIf all of those tests pass then I will be satisfied.  ...but we need to figure out what boards had what version of rk808 and why we weren\u0027t informed of this change earlier.",
